{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"OESA-2026-3050","published":"2026-07-19T03:49:05Z","modified":"2026-07-19T04:00:19.626795961Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-12184","CVE-2026-14355"],"summary":"php security update","details":"PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts. The php package contains the module (often referred to as mod_php) which adds support for the PHP language to Apache HTTP Server.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n(CVE-2026-12184)\n\nIn PHP versions 8.2.* before 8.2.32, 8.3.* before 8.3.32, 8.4.* before 8.4.23, 8.5.* before 8.5.8, the AES-WRAP-PAD algorithm implementation in OpenSSL extension contains a buffer allocation flaw. The output buffer for the AES key-wrap-with-padding operation is sized from the plaintext length without accounting for RFC 5649 expansion. This may cause OpenSSL to write beyond allocated memory, corrupting heap metadata and triggering application abort.(CVE-2026-14355)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"php","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/php&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["php-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-bcmath-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-cli-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-common-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-dba-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-dbg-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-debuginfo-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-debugsource-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-devel-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-embedded-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","php-enchant-8.3.32-1.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","